{
  "mode": "no_defect",
  "understanding": "This procedure manages the front brake service for the Segway Xyber, requiring a pad thickness check, caliper cleaning, bolt torquing, and photographic verification. Over the examined window, the procedure successfully identified worn pads below the minimum threshold in several jobs while passing those that met the criteria, with all steps completed without blockage.",
  "jobs_examined": 20,
  "findings": [],
  "considered_and_rejected": [
    "We observed that Step 1 ('Check the pads before you touch anything') failed in 9 out of 20 jobs (J-4500 through J-4508) because the measured pad thickness was 1.4 mm, which is below the 2 mm limit. This is not a procedure defect; it is the procedure correctly identifying worn components that require replacement, which is the intended safety behavior of the check."
  ]
}
